284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (The Segment Anything Model \(SAM\) is a versatile image segmentation model that uses prompt engineering to handle various tasks and enable zero-shot transfer. It combines an image encoder, prompt encoder, and mask decoder, trained on a massive dataset \(SA-1B\) with over 1 billion masks from 11 million images.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 206 0 R
/T (SAM \(Segment Anything Model\) leverages zero-shot learning, enabling it to generalize to new tasks and datasets without additional training. Fine-tuning SAM involves adjusting its parameters on specific datasets to enhance performance for particular segmentation tasks. While zero-shot learning allows SAM to perform well on a broad range of tasks using prompt engineering, fine-tuning can further improve its accuracy and adaptability to specific applications by optimizing the model based on targeted data.)
/E (SAM \(Segment Anything Model\) leverages zero-shot learning, enabling it to generalize to new tasks and datasets without additional training. Fine-tuning SAM involves adjusting its parameters on specific datasets to enhance performance for particular segmentation tasks. While zero-shot learning allows SAM to perform well on a broad range of tasks using prompt engineering, fine-tuning can further improve its accuracy and adaptability to specific applications by optimizing the model based on targeted data.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
