1341 0 obj
<<
/Title (SAM \(Segment Anything Model\) leverages zero-shot learning, enabling it to generalize to new tasks and datasets without additional training. Fine-tuning SAM involves adjusting its parameters on specific datasets to enhance performance for particular segmentation tasks. While zero-shot learning allows SAM to perform well on a broad range of tasks using prompt engineering, fine-tuning can further improve its accuracy and adaptability to specific applications by optimizing the model based on targeted data.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1331 0 R
>>
endobj
1342 0 obj
<<
/Title (SAM was trained with 11 million images, producing through the data engine, 1.1B masks, which produces the SA-1B dataset. The mask decoder is what is generally fine-tuned, since we want to go through the parts that directly interact with specific prompts and segmentation tasks. Fine-tuning this parts ensures that our model can behave better on a more specific task.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1333 0 R
/First 1349 0 R
/Last 1349 0 R
/Count -1
>>
